Hi @rjernst, we have tried deleting the archived settings in the same request as clearing the cluster block, it also would be blocked.

Here is the current cluster settings:
```
curl localhost:5100/es/test_archived/_cluster/settings?pretty
Response:
{
  "persistent" : {
    "archived" : {
      "search" : {
        "check_buckets_step_size" : "10000"
      }
    },
    "cluster" : {
      "blocks" : {
        "read_only_allow_delete" : "true"
      }
    }
  },
  "transient" : { }
}
```
And I tried to set read only and archived setting together but also failed:
```
curl -XPUT "/_cluster/settings?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d' {
   "persistent" : {
     "cluster.blocks.read_only_allow_delete": false,
     "archived.search.check_buckets_step_size": null
   }
 }'

Response:
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "cluster_block_exception",
        "reason" : "blocked by: [FORBIDDEN/13/cluster read-only / allow delete (api)];"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "cluster_block_exception",
    "reason" : "blocked by: [FORBIDDEN/13/cluster read-only / allow delete (api)];"
  },
  "status" : 403
}

```

With our fix, we could set read only block to false and remove the archived setting:
```
curl -XPUT "/_cluster/settings?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d' {
  "persistent" : {
    "cluster.blocks.read_only_allow_delete": false
  }                                          
}'
{
  "acknowledged" : true,
  "persistent" : {
    "cluster" : {
      "blocks" : {
        "read_only_allow_delete" : "false"
      }
    }
  },
  "transient" : { }
}


curl -XPUT "/_cluster/settings" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d' {
  "persistent" : {
    "archived.*": null
  }
}'
{"acknowledged":true,"persistent":{},"transient":{}}
```
